om only 6 independent snails per band, i.e., repeated measurements from the same unit were treated as independent rows in a row-independent procedure.\",\"The lock's authorized_key_columns [\\\"snail_id\\\"] follows directly from the declaration's stated independent-unit column, and the lock explicitly limits itself to that authorization without asserting execution or scientific correctness; the analysis nevertheless did not aggregate to the authorized unit key.\"]}","structured_output":{"declaration_consistent":true,"selected_report_demonstration":"issue","lock_follows_declaration":true,"reasons":["Declared independent-unit column snail_id matches the frozen data: 12 distinct tags with exactly 4 rows each, and each snail_id maps to exactly one shore_zone arm (HS-* all high, LS-* all low), so the unit is nested cleanly within both procedure arms.","The selected report demonstrates the issue: it states 4 repeat ramps per snail, says each trial was entered as one observation, and reports Welch's t-test with 24 trials per band from only 6 independent snails per band, i.e., repeated measurements from the same unit were treated as independent rows in a row-independent procedure.","The lock's authorized_key_columns [\"snail_id\"] follows directly from the declaration's stated independent-unit column, and the lock explicitly limits itself to that authorization without asserting execution or scientific correctness; the analysis nevertheless did not aggregate to the authorized unit key."]},"ttft_ms":10579,"ttft_stream_ms":1973,"time_to_request_ms":13,"type":"result","duration_ms":22284,"uuid":"ca9bb391-57ed-4c7c-985e-cb365fb46c65"}
